According to a report by Intel Market Research, Global laser anti sniper detection system market size was valued at USD 350 million in 2025. The market is forecasted to grow from USD 420 million in 2026 to USD 950 million by 2034, exhibiting a CAGR of 10.8 % during the forecast period.
Laser anti sniper detection systems are advanced optical and sensor solutions designed to identify hostile sniper fire and provide real time alerts for homeland security forces. These systems combine lidar, infrared imaging, acoustic triangulation and AI driven analytics to locate shooters within seconds, enabling rapid counter measures and enhanced force protection across critical infrastructure, urban policing zones and forward operating bases.
The market expands because governments are allocating larger budgets toward counter terrorism technologies, recent high profile sniping incidents have heightened public safety concerns, and sensor miniaturization has reduced deployment costs. Notable activity includes a July 2023 contract awarded by the U.S. Department of Defense for a next generation lidar platform from Raytheon Technologies, while European security agencies have begun trials of AI enhanced acoustic arrays supplied by Thales Group.
